DESCRIPTION:Strum\, sing\, and laugh your way through a week of beginner u
 kulele fun\, designed especially for kids. With easy chords\, familiar son
 gs\, and group play\, children build skills and confidence while discoveri
 ng the joy of making music together. No experience required! This program 
 is presented in collaboration with the Toronto Blues Society.\nUkuleles wi
 ll be provided.\nFor children ages 8-12.\nRegistration begins February 2\,
  2026.\nPlease make sure you can commit to all five sessions (March 16 - M
 arch 20\, 10 - 11 am) before registering.\nInformation Collection Notice:
 \nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public
  Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(
 d). The information will only be used for event and program registration\,
  delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your inf
 ormation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416
 -397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
