BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gardiner Museum": "https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/single-class-for-families-march-18-2026/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gardiner_museum
X-SOURCE:Gardiner Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260318T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260318T180000
DTSTAMP:20260316T021431
CREATED:20260220T225128Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260220T225334Z
UID:142623-1773849600-1773856800@www.gardinermuseum.on.ca
SUMMARY:Single Class: For Families
DESCRIPTION:Single Class: For Families            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n				\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Wednesday March 18\, 2026\n4:00 pm – 6:00 pm\n \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Get creative with clay this March Break! Families can work together using hand-building techniques to create decorative sculptures\, guided by an experienced artist-educator in a professional ceramics studio. Instruction is provided at the beginner level. \nChoose a ticket for two (2) participants (One child ages 5 – 13 and one adult 18+) or three (3) participants (Two children ages 5 – 13 and one adult 18+). \nYour ticket includes access to earthenware clay\, underglazes\, and a variety of tools\, as well as the firing of one work per participant. Additional firings are $10 per piece. This class does not include glazing. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                General : $60\n                             \n                1 Adult + 1 Child\n                          \n                        \n               \n                General : $90\n                             \n                1 Adult + 2 Children\n                          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $51\n                             \n                1 Adult + 1 Child\n                          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $76.50\n                             \n                1 Adult + 2 Children\n                          \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                                Get Tickets\n              \n                        \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information \nTicketholders\, including Students and Gardiner Friends\, will be asked to produce ID when checking in for the class. Discount does not apply to Get Acquainted pass holders. Friends may only purchase at the discounted rate for Friendship card holders. \nTickets for this class are non-refundable and non-transferable\, regardless of reason. Due to the volume of requests and the small size of our team\, we are unable to respond to or accommodate requests for refunds or transfers at this time. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class Policies: \nThe hand building demonstration will begin 5 minutes into the class. The final 30 minutes of the class are for clean up. \nWorks made in this class are decorative and not food safe. \nBy signing up for this class\, participants are committing to abide by the Museum’s Code of Conduct and Studio Policies\, which can be found here. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Firing and Pick Up: \nWorks are fired in our electric kilns and will be ready for pick up two (2) weeks after your class. \nFired pieces can ONLY be picked up on Saturdays and Sundays from 10 am – 4:30 pm. No exceptions. \nWorks will be held at the Museum for two months from the date of your class\, after which they will be disposed of or donated. Please check in at the Front Desk when you arrive to pick up your work. We do not provide packing materials\, bags\, or boxes to carry your works. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/single-class-for-families-march-18-2026/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Kids Classes,Programs & Events
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/wp-content/uploads/Family-Days-Thumbnail-1.jpeg
GEO:43.6679938;-79.3935128
