CREATED:20260215T033422Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260215T033422Z
UID:8288-1774384200-1774393200@jazzbistro.ca
SUMMARY:Riverrun
DESCRIPTION:Tom Richards – keys and composition\nPeter Lutek – space clarinet\nKae Murphy – trumpet *special guest*\nScott Peterson – bass\nJake Oelrichs – drums\nBrandon Valdivia – percussion *special guest*\n\n\n\nRiverrun is a collection of some of Toronto’s strongest musical personalities\, led by keyboardist and composer Tom Richards. Cinematic\, delving and disciplined\, Riverrun cuts across stylistic boundaries and goes deep into the moment. \n\nCOVER: $20
URL:https://jazzbistro.ca/event/riverrun/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a5d55c403a4e5652ddf155"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Cuban & Brazilian Drumming
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260324T203000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260324T213000Z
UID:69a5d55c403a4e5652ddf155@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A lively drumming program highlighting two of the most influen
 tial countries in world music\, Cuba and Brazil\, both culturally rich in 
 rhythms and songs. Experience the exciting music of traditional cultural e
 vents like Carnival and community festivals led by ​professional drummer
  and percussionist\, Joaquin Nunez Hidalgo.\nAll teens are welcome! Drop-i
 n\, no registration required.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. 
 Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school and in the summer\
 , where helpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious snacks are 
 offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to 
 find out more.
LOCATION:Northern District\, Youth Hub (on the second floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a5d55c403a4e5652ddf155
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698f73898d5e2d09335efd78"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Pitch & Storytelling Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260324T210000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260324T220000Z
UID:698f73898d5e2d09335efd78@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This interactive workshop is all about helping you level up yo
 ur pitching skills!\nLearn to turn your ideas into powerful stories\, grab
  people’s attention\, and explain what you do in a clear and exciting wa
 y.\nCreate a strong “elevator pitch” — a short\, memorable intro you
  can use anytime\, anywhere — and make a lasting impression on any audie
 nce.\nDrop-in. Limited spots.\nThis is part of the Youth for Entrepreneurs
 hip program led by the YMCA of Greater Toronto. Through hands-on sessions\
 , you’ll gain the digital tools\, financial knowledge\, and creative str
 ategies needed to build a business idea from the ground up.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Auditorium (lower level)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698f73898d5e2d09335efd78
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"UofT Engineering": "https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/event/online-info-session-civmin-mengcem-program/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:uoft_engineering
X-SOURCE:UofT Engineering
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260324T211500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260324T221500
DTSTAMP:20260313T214425
CREATED:20260312T210031Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260312T210104Z
UID:10004436-1774386900-1774390500@www.engineering.utoronto.ca
SUMMARY:Online Info Session: CivMin MEngCEM Program
DESCRIPTION:Tuesday\, March 24\, 9:15-10:15 p.m. ET\nOnline via Zoom \nDiscover how a Master of Engineering in Cities Engineering & Management (MEngCEM) degree in Civil & Mineral Engineering at U of T can unlock new possibilities and accelerate your career growth! \nFrom our exciting courses to the dynamic hands-on learning offered through a 4-month practicum\, our MEngCEM program offers the opportunity to build expertise in how urban systems drive prosperity\, assess risks to critical infrastructure policy\, and apply evidence-based management to address complex city challenges worldwide. \nJoin Associate Chair Sebastian Goodfellow\, Professor Shoshanna Saxe and Adam Hasham to learn about our MEngCEM and how you can customize your program to align with your professional goals. \nRegister here to get the Zoom link
URL:https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/event/online-info-session-civmin-mengcem-program/
LOCATION:Zoom
CATEGORIES:Info sessions
END:VEVENT
