SUMMARY:Coding with Python IV
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260324T220000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260325T000000Z
UID:6974f14a834cbb3dea290d46@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Python is an open source programming language that is used for
  creating web applications\, web content\, mathematics and system scriptin
 g. In this follow up course we will take our understanding of data structu
 res to the next level as well as looking into the next stages of error han
 dling (including making some custom error messages) and extending our know
 ledge of input/output to more than just the terminal.\nThis class is for b
 eginners but assumes you have a basic understanding of Python or have atte
 nded Coding with Python I\, II\, and III.\nRegistration will start 2 weeks
  before this class. Computers will be provided.\nInformation Collection No
 tice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto P
 ublic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, an
 d 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registrat
 ion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles you
 r information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\
 , 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Riverdale\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6974f14a834cbb3dea290d46
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
