DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260325T210000Z
UID:699df5f581b67dfe32a88f4f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Teens will get the opportunity to handle and examine nine real
  and replica dinosaur fossils in this fun\, hands-on workshop! Teens will 
 learn about dinosaurs\, evolution\, fossilization\, and phylogeny\; while 
 they examine fossilized dinosaur footprints\, woolly mammoth tooth\, and m
 ore! All materials will be provided\; this is a drop-in program.\nThis pro
 gram is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for te
 ens after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always availa
 ble. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a
 \nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
