DESCRIPTION:The City of Toronto is honored to host biologist Natasha Gonsa
 lves from the Toronto and Region Conservation Authority for an engaging we
 binar on grasses and grass-like plants. Discover the intricacies of identi
 fying these elusive yet abundant plants within our urban ecosystem. Come w
 ith your curiosities and leave with the ability to distinguish between rus
 hes\, sedges and grasses\, along with common examples of each and an under
 standing of their precious role in local habitats and landscapes. Grass ID
 's not just a field of dreams\, it’s a field of facts.\nCategories: Envi
 ronmental\, Talks\, Virtual/Online Event\nFree event
