DTSTART:20260326T180000Z
DTEND:20260326T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260316T061721Z
UID:trrfe4h99ogksl8vj4lmd8ib0c@google.com
CREATED:20250814T203832Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Title: <b>The Black Hole Diet: How Accretion Controls Spin\,
  Growth\, and Feedback</b></p>\n\n<p>Abstract: A black hole’s accretion rat
 e controls its destiny\, governing its spin\, growth\, luminosity\, and fee
 dback. However\, connecting these crucial quantities to the scales we can a
 ctually observe\, remains a major theoretical hurdle. In this talk\, I will
  present recent simulations of magnetized gas feeding rapidly rotating blac
 k holes. These models offer new insights into the mechanics of gas consumpt
 ion and ejection. I will demonstrate how these findings apply to a vast ran
 ge of systems\, linking the physics of supermassive black holes at the cent
 ers of galaxies to stellar-mass black holes born in dying stars.\n</p>\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260310T204425Z
LOCATION:1318A
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Alexander (Sasha) Tchekhovskoy (Northwestern University)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
