SUMMARY:Healthy Eating Series
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260330T150000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260330T160000Z
UID:6966accc8b29ea2800c93e6f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Healthy Eating Series by Toronto Public Health for Birth to Si
 x years by Toronto Public Health\, presented in partnership with Working W
 omen Community Centre.\nThese workshops are designed for\nparents and care
 givers of children from birth to 6 years\nand will be led by Azar Mehrabia
 n\, Community Nutrition Educator with Toronto Public Health.\nAll adults a
 nd seniors are welcome!\nThe workshop topics are:\nMarch 16: Healthy Lunc
 hes and Snacks\, 11 AM - 12 PM:\nKey consideration when planning healthy l
 unches & snacks for children 2 to 6 years\nQuick and healthy lunch and sna
 ck ideas\nFood safety tips when packing lunches and snacks\nMarch 30: Mea
 ltime Environments and Feeding Relationship\,\n11 AM - 12 PM:\nHealthy eat
 ing environment and feeding relationship\nCommon feeding challenges for to
 ddlers and preschoolers and tips to overcome them\nHow to allow children t
 o follow their hunger and fullness cues\nHow to involve children in food s
 kills\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this fo
 rm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries A
 ct\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used
  for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions a
 bout how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerlin
 e staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toront
 o ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6966accc8b29ea2800c93e6f
