BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Botanical Garden": "https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/how-can-gardeners-support-nature/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_botanical
X-SOURCE:Toronto Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260402T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260402T200000
DTSTAMP:20260316T021437
CREATED:20260223T175724Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260224T205830Z
UID:10001939-1775156400-1775160000@torontobotanicalgarden.ca
SUMMARY:How Can Gardeners Support Nature?
DESCRIPTION:Learn about the work that Toronto Nature Stewards are doing and how you can help!\n\n\nImagine you are a butterfly hovering over Toronto\, searching for a safe place to rest\, feed\, and lay your eggs. You spot a patch of green in the urban jungle\, but when you land\, the plants you depend on aren’t there. \nHow can Toronto residents help protect nature? What do gardeners need to understand about invasive species? Learn about Toronto Nature Stewards—what they’re doing to care for our city’s ecosystems\, and how you can get involved. \nThursday\, April 2 from 7 to 8 p.m. \nPublic $20\, TBG Members $15 (plus applicable taxes and fees). \nAbout John Oyston \nJohn Oyston has volunteered with Toronto Nature Stewards (TNS) for 4 years and has been Lead Steward at their Leaside Park location for 3 yearrs. \nA retired physician\, he also holds the Ontario Diploma in Horticulture. He served as Vice President of the North American Native Plant Society and is currently on the Board of Dont Mess with the Don. He has a100 acre nature reserve\, Oak Hills Farm\, located south of Peterbrough. \nToronto Nature Stewards works with the City of Toronto to remove garbage and invasive plants\, and replant native species\, at over 50 locations across Toronto. \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member ! \nAdditional Program Information\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/how-can-gardeners-support-nature/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Avenue East\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Gardening
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/f32cf0bb9640886b91878648a704bd57.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"City of Toronto Festivals & Events": "https://www.rcmusic.com/events-and-performances/orchestra-baobab"}
X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_festivals
SUMMARY:Orchestra Baobab with Special Guest Mis Blandine
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260402T190000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260402T190000
UID:20f083b144010c70f90e73182afd39c2@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Known as West Africa’s greatest band\, Senegal’s very own 
 brings their mix of Afro-Cuban style\, international pop\, traditional gri
 ot music\, and mellifluous rhythms to Koerner Hall. Congolese rumba opens 
 the night.\n\nFor 55 years\, Orchestra Baobab has filled venues and festiv
 als across the globe with dancing crowds. Their success story began in Dak
 ar\, where the group picked up Cuban styles like son and pachanga. Startin
 g at Club Baobab\, built around the iconic tree\, the group travelled exte
 nsively through West Africa. All kinds of influences were integrated into 
 the "Baobab sound" and the band continues to make their sound more thrilli
 ng than ever with lively twists and energetic additions.\n\nCategories: Cu
 ltural\, Live Performances\, Music
LOCATION:Koerner Hall\, Royal Conservatory of Music\, 273 Bloor St W\, Tor
 onto\, ON\, M5S 1W2
URL:https://www.rcmusic.com/events-and-performances/orchestra-baobab
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
