LAST-MODIFIED:20251212T230543Z
UID:140854-1775584800-1775588400@www.gardinermuseum.on.ca
SUMMARY:Uncertain Ground: Curator Tour with Sequoia Miller
DESCRIPTION:Uncertain Ground: Curator Tour with Sequoia Miller            \n                                    \n                                \n                        \n                                                \n                                                        Get Tickets                        \n                                            \n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n	\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Tuesday April 7\, 2026\n6:00 pm – 7:00 pm\n \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Join Chief Curator & Deputy Director Sequoia Miller for an inside look at the exhibition Linda Rotua Sormin: Uncertain Ground. Explore the stories\, materials\, and ideas that shape Sormin’s immersive ceramic installations\, from fragments and found objects to questions of place\, identity\, and belonging. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                General : $35\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $30\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                    Add to cart\n\n                    \n\n\n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    About the Exhibition \nLinda Rotua Sormin: Uncertain Ground is the culmination of over 20 years of remarkable exploration and innovation\, bringing together clay\, sculpture\, video\, sound\, hand-cut watercolour painting\, and digital fabrication in a multi-sensory environment that asks how life in the modern\, cosmopolitan city can coexist with memories and experiences of our ancestral traditions. \nThe exhibition unfolds on three levels: a central raised platform evokes a volcanic lake with an underworld of mythical beasts and coded divination texts; a tangle of precarious ceramic sculptures suggests an earthly middle ground inhabited by humans; and a suspended projection screen references a celestial realm of spirits and birds. The result is an environment that feels alive and in motion\, offering audiences an encounter that is both visceral and contemplative.\nLearn more \n  \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/uncertain-ground-curator-tour-with-sequoia-miller-april-7-2026/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Programs & Events
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/wp-content/uploads/Sequoia-Sormin-Tour-1.jpg
GEO:43.6679938;-79.3935128
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Gardiner Museum 111 Queen's Park Toronto ON M5S 2C7 Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=111 Queen's Park:geo:-79.3935128,43.6679938
END:VEVENT
