SUMMARY:Social Assistance in Ontario: An Overview of OW & ODSP
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260407T180000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260407T193000Z
UID:6994d42b7d180d0d4833ec0e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join Downsview Community Legal Services (DCLS) for monthly leg
 al information sessions. Learn more about the law and discuss your legal r
 ights. Each session will explore a different topic.\nThis workshop will go
  over the requirements to apply for Ontario Works (OW) and Ontario Disabil
 ity Support Program (ODSP)\, how to apply\, and how to challenge decisions
  about social assistance benefits. Spousal support and income deductions w
 hile on social assistance will also be covered.\nRegistration is encourage
 d.\nDrop-ins are welcome until capacity is reached.\nInformation Collectio
 n Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toron
 to Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\
 , and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regis
 tration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles
  your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.c
 a\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101\, Ground floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6994d42b7d180d0d4833ec0e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
