SUMMARY:A Daughter’s Place by Martha Batiz - By the Lake Book Club 
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260414T190000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260414T190000
UID:6d82e23fb3166d9e7faeb9568c79741d@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:A Daughter’s Place\, the debut novel by award-winning author
  Martha Bátiz\, is a sweeping historical narrative set in the Spanish Gol
 den Age. Inspired by the real-life daughter of Miguel de Cervantes\, the b
 ook follows fifteen-year-old Isabel as she navigates secrecy\, love\, and 
 survival in a patriarchal world while her father works on Don Quixote. Thr
 ough richly detailed prose\, Bátiz gives voice to the women who lived in 
 the shadows of history\, blending drama\, resilience and untold stories.\n
 \nBy the Lake Book Club hosts six Tuesday-night events from February to De
 cember with top Canadian authors and Humber Polytechnics alumni. Each in-p
 erson event features readings\, discussions\, Q&A\, book signings and ASL 
 interpretation\, while virtual sessions include live subtitles and audio a
 ccess.\nCategories: Literary
LOCATION:Assembly Hall\, 1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr\, Etobicoke\, ON\,
  M8V 4B6
URL:https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-cent
 res-galleries/assembly-hall/
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
