SUMMARY:Adobe Lightroom
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260415T220000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260415T233000Z
UID:69b07d021e64afd01e6136c0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn the basics of working with Adobe Lightroom. Crop\, edit 
 and organize photos with this industry standard program.\nIn this introduc
 tion to Lightroom you will learn how to: work with the Library Panel\, imp
 ort your photos\, basic editing in the Develop Module and common editing o
 perations: crop & straighten\, sharpen a blurry picture\, reduce haze\, ra
 dial filters \, enhanced spot remover and save and export pictures\nCreate
  an Adobe account before class at:\nhttp://account.adobe.com/account\nRegi
 stration is required for this class. You can order free tickets by clickin
 g the link below. Tickets will become available one week prior to the clas
 s at 9 a.m.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on t
 his form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libra
 ries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only b
 e used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Quest
 ions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Ans
 werline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, 
 Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b07d021e64afd01e6136c0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
