BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"City of Toronto Festivals & Events": "http://toronto.ca/marketgallery"}
X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_festivals
SUMMARY:Smoke Signals x Reflections
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260416T180000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260613T120000
UID:1220686304a8dabf07ed7f800bf19885@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Visit Smoke Signals x Reflections presented by TD Bank Group a
 nd Toronto History Museums\, an exhibition where photography\, beadwork\, 
 sculpture and digital media serve as a guiding signal\, broadcasting stori
 es of identity\, memory and reconnection. \n\nCurated by Jesse King\, the 
 exhibit shares pieces from Toronto’s Fine Art and Artifact Collection\, 
 including the photographic series The Emergence of Legend by Kent Monkman 
 as well as contemporary art by Alexis Nanibush-Pamajewong\, Jake Kimble\, 
 Kay Nadjiwon\, Kiki Guerard\, Megan Feheley and Melissa Johns. Expect bold
  visuals\, self-discovery\, and personal storytelling.\n \nSmoke Signals x
  Reflections aims to create a safe and affirming space for two-spirit\, In
 digi-queer\, and gender nonconforming artists.\n\nCategories: Arts/Exhibit
 s\, Museum\nFree event
LOCATION:401 Richmond Ltd\, 401 Richmond Street West\, Suite 128
URL:http://toronto.ca/marketgallery
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
