SUMMARY:After School Club: The Play's the Thing! - Theatre Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260416T200000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260416T210000Z
UID:698b5ac22a787a47a5e6fcfb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join our guest\, writer and producer Jodi Crawford who will le
 ad kids to take ownership of every element of creating their very own play
  or puppet show\, from set decoration to costume or puppet making to scrip
 t writing to performance. Incorporating movement activities\, group collab
 oration\, and artistic expression\, this program can help children with co
 nfidence and allows them to work to their individual strengths. For childr
 en 6-12 years.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information o
 n this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Li
 braries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will onl
 y be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Qu
 estions about how the library handles your information can be directed to 
 Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street
 \, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Pape/Danforth\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698b5ac22a787a47a5e6fcfb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698f747481b67dfe32a63df9"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Branding
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260416T210000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260416T220000Z
UID:698f747481b67dfe32a63df9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Ready to build a brand that’s 100% YOU?\nIn this workshop\, 
 you’ll discover what makes you unique and how to show it with confidence
 . Learn how to create your own brand from scratch—write a strong mission
  statement\, choose your core values\, and set brand guidelines so your vi
 be stays consistent.\nCheck out real businesses started by young entrepren
 eurs just like you—and see how their ideas turned into success stories. 
 Your idea could be next.\nThis workshop is part of the Youth for Entrepren
 eurship program led by the YMCA of Greater Toronto. Through hands-on sessi
 ons\, you’ll gain the digital tools\, financial knowledge\, and creative
  strategies needed to build a business idea from the ground up.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Auditorium (lower level)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698f747481b67dfe32a63df9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699761f88b29ea2800d11b95"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Photo Editing with Photoshop
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260416T220000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260417T000000Z
UID:699761f88b29ea2800d11b95@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Adobe Photoshop is the world’s best imaging and graphic desi
 gn software and is at the core of just about every creative project\, from
  photo editing and compositing to digital painting\, animation\, and graph
 ic design.\nJoin us for an introductory lesson and learn about the most co
 mmon tools. We'll explore the workspace and enhance images while investiga
 ting tools such as crop\, levels\, colour balance and more. See how an ima
 ge can be altered and repaired using patch tools such as the clone and hea
 ling brush tools. We'll also dive deep into the world of layers and how yo
 u can manage them for those really unique and fun projects.\nRegistration 
 is required.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on 
 this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libr
 aries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only 
 be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Ques
 tions about how the library handles your information can be directed to An
 swerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\,
  Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Basement (Room B/C)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699761f88b29ea2800d11b95
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f5cc78b29ea2800d27a09"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Throwback Thursdays: Great Movies on the Big Screen
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260416T220000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260417T000000Z
UID:699f5cc78b29ea2800d27a09@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come join us for a radical retro rewind projected on the big s
 creen. Whether you're a first-time viewer or long-time fan\, these movies 
 are sure to please.\nFebruary 26: If Beale Street Could Talk (2018\, 14A)
 \nMarch 5: The Social Network (2010\, PG)\nMarch 12: Steve Jobs (2015\, R
 )\nMarch 19: Michael Clayton (2007\, 14A)\nMarch 26: Ocean’s Twelve (2
 004\, PG)\nAll are welcome. Drop-in\, no registration required.
LOCATION:High Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f5cc78b29ea2800d27a09
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b309bb81b67dfe32ac20c5"}
