SUMMARY:Learn to Make a Video Game
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260416T220000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260417T000000Z
UID:69b309bb81b67dfe32ac20c5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn to make a 2D Platformer using the free browser-based vid
 eo game development tool : Construct 3\nLearn the basics of video game dev
 elopment using Construct 3\, a free browser-based game engine. In this ses
 sion you'll learn how to create a 2D platformer without the need for codin
 g. Participants will learn the interface and tools of the software\, and b
 y the end of the class will have built their own simple game.\nRegistratio
 n is required.\nRegistration begins on April 7th at 12:30pm.\nNote: Your s
 pot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nI
 nformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is co
 llected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sec
 tions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for eve
 nt and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how
  the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff 
 at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W
  2G8
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor - eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b309bb81b67dfe32ac20c5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699b3fd74dacf581ff7d12e7"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Sea of Life: Documentary for National Canadian Film Day
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260416T220000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260416T233000Z
UID:699b3fd74dacf581ff7d12e7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Sea of Life is a 2017 documentary film about filmmaker Julia B
 arnes' journey around the world to save the ecosystems we depend on\, as 
 we come closer to causing a mass extinction in the oceans.\nScheduled for 
 the day after National Canadian Film Day\, in this documentary\, Barnes t
 akes a deep dive into how actions by governments\, businesses and ordinary
  people can all have a drastic impact on sustainability\nThanks to\nReel C
 anada\nfor providing the screening of this film.\nRun time: 88 minutes
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699b3fd74dacf581ff7d12e7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b2f65db48451fc3c086dbe"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Investing 101: What You Need to Know
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260416T230000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260417T000000Z
UID:69b2f65db48451fc3c086dbe@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Whether you are starting out or learning more about your curre
 nt investments\, this seminar will help you make sense of the complex worl
 d of investing. We will cover the three asset classes: stocks\, bonds\, an
 d cash plus simple ways to get started with investing. In this easy-to-und
 erstand seminar\, Teri will set out the advantages of each of the three ma
 jor tax-sheltered investing plans for Canadians: Tax-Free Savings Accounts
  (TFSAs)\, Registered Retirement Savings Plans (RRSPs) and the new First H
 ome Savings Accounts (FHSAs).\nPresented by Teri Courchene\, BA\, MA\, M
 Ed\, CSC. Teri is a former investing instructor at U of T School of Conti
 nuing Studies and former director of economic research at a major bank. On
 e of her current volunteer roles is giving investing and finance talks at 
 Toronto Public Library branches.
LOCATION:Pape/Danforth\, 2nd floor program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b2f65db48451fc3c086dbe
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
