DESCRIPTION:Diamond painting is a relaxing craft that combines paint-by-nu
 mbers and mosaics\, allowing you to create shimmering\, 3D masterpieces by
  applying tiny resin "diamonds" to a coded\, adhesive canvas. It is a medi
 tative\, low-mess activity that reduces stress\, making it accessible to b
 eginners and experienced crafters alike.\nRegistration is required. For a
 ges 7-12 only (children outside of this age range will not be able to part
 icipate).\n*For all registered Children's programs at Malvern\, there is a
  grace period of 10 minutes. After the first 10 minutes of a program\, spo
 ts will be given to waiting customers.*\nInformation Collection Notice:\nT
 he personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Li
 brary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d).
  The information will only be used for event and program registration\, de
 livery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your inform
 ation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-39
 7-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Community room.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69af3c2381b67dfe32ab7918
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b04d85ec71a31f5b428b96"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Classic Tiramisu Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260422T200000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260422T210000Z
UID:69b04d85ec71a31f5b428b96@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn the basics of how to make the classic Italian dessert\, 
 Tiramisu. Chef Yumiko will provide and explain all the ingredients and tak
 e the participants through a simple step-by-step process of creating a del
 icious ready-to-eat dish.\nFood allergy notice: Please be aware that food 
 will be used in this program that include dairy\, wheat flour\, egg and de
 caffeinated espresso.  The audience should be advised that certain food in
 gredients may cause allergic reactions in some people.\nThis program is pa
 rt of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after 
 school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always available. Free
 \, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hu
 b\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Youth Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b04d85ec71a31f5b428b96
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
