BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b5a549b48451fc3c08e82c"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:GameOn: Life Skills Through Soccer
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260422T210000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260422T220000Z
UID:69b5a549b48451fc3c08e82c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Stay confident under pressure\, and connect better with others
 . It's all about building skills\, making friends\, and growing as a playe
 r and a leader through soccer.\nPepy Malonga is the founder of FOOT-IQ\, a
 n educational initiative that uses sport as a platform to help young peopl
 e develop leadership and life skills. Through interactive workshops and yo
 uth programs\, he helps participants explore themes such as communication\
 , teamwork\, decision-making\, and emotional intelligence using engaging s
 port-based scenarios and discussions.\nPepy has led programs with schools\
 , libraries\, and community organizations across Toronto\, creating enviro
 nments where youth build confidence\, reflect on their choices\, and stren
 gthen their leadership potential.\nHis work focuses on helping young peopl
 e understand that leadership is not about performance\, but about mindset\
 , responsibility\, and how they interact with others.\nRegistration requir
 ed. Drop-ins welcome\, but space is limited\n.
LOCATION:Beaches\, Program Room or outdoors (weather permitting)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b5a549b48451fc3c08e82c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ab2b5d6724c63d00f732cf"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Photo Editing with Photoshop
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260422T220000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260422T233000Z
UID:69ab2b5d6724c63d00f732cf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Adobe Photoshop is the world’s best imaging and graphic desi
 gn software and is at the core of just about every creative project\, from
  photo editing and compositing to digital painting\, animation\, and graph
 ic design.\nJoin us for an introductory lesson and learn about the most co
 mmon tools. We'll explore the workspace and enhance images while investiga
 ting tools such as crop\, levels\, colour balance and more. See how an ima
 ge can be altered and repaired using patch tools such as the clone and hea
 ling brush tools. We'll also dive deep into the world of layers and how yo
 u can manage them for those really unique and fun projects.\nRegistration 
 is required.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on 
 this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libr
 aries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only 
 be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Ques
 tions about how the library handles your information can be directed to An
 swerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\,
  Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:New Toronto\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ab2b5d6724c63d00f732cf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
