BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"City of Toronto Festivals & Events": "https://toronto.webex.com/webappng/sites/toronto/webinar/webinarSeries/register/cee2b157aad54ef6a36e8a38e5ad515b"}
X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_festivals
SUMMARY:Native Edible Plants of Toronto Webinar
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260423T120000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260423T120000
UID:ea2860ffa879a76175eb3afb6469c8d2@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Blueberries\, raspberries\, strawberries: they aren’t just f
 ound at the grocery store. There are native species of these fruits found 
 in Toronto’s ravines too!  Join avid fruit gardener and City of Toronto
  Forestry staffer Steven Parkes for a webinar on Toronto’s native and ed
 ible fruiting plants\, their ecological importance and where you might spo
 t them in our urban wilderness. You’ll learn how adding these plants to 
 your local landscapes and private gardens can enhance habitats\, support l
 ocal wildlife and pollinators\, while producing native fruits and nuts. Pl
 ease note: this is not a foraging webinar. The focus will be on integratin
 g native edible plants into private gardens. Please snack responsibly.\nCa
 tegories: Environmental\, Talks\, Virtual/Online Event\nFree event
LOCATION:On-line Event
URL:https://toronto.webex.com/webappng/sites/toronto/webinar/webinarSeries
 /register/cee2b157aad54ef6a36e8a38e5ad515b
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
