BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"City of Toronto Festivals & Events": "https://musictorontoconcerts.com/concerts/isserlis-shin"}
X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_festivals
SUMMARY:Steven Isserlis\, cello and Connie Shih\, piano
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260423T193000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260423T193000
UID:ab90329d354b34a5e1e5659326a15efd@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:These celebrated musicians are frequent collaborators\, captiv
 ating audiences at world-class venues like Wigmore Hall\, Carnegie Hall\, 
 and the Berlin Philharmonie. \n\nBeyond performance\, Isserlis is a passio
 nate teacher\, author\, and broadcaster. As Sir John Barbirolli said\, “
 Steven Isserlis is a musician of immense talent and insight\, whose sound 
 and interpretation leave a deep and lasting impression.”\n\nTheir though
 tfully curated program highlights Isserlis’s broad musical interests\, f
 eaturing the Ritournelle by Czech composer Vítězslava Kaprálová alongs
 ide beloved cello-piano repertoire gems. The program also includes Beethov
 en’s 12 Variations on a Theme from The Magic Flute\, Op. 66 and Sonata N
 o. 3 in A major\, Op. 69\, Schumann’s 3 Fantasiestücke\, Op. 73\, and K
 abalevsky’s Sonata. Experience an exceptional evening of profound musici
 anship and emotional depth from this outstanding duo.\n\nCategories: Cultu
 ral\, Live Performances\, Music
LOCATION:Jane Mallett Theatre\, St. Lawrence Centre for the Arts\, 27 Fron
 t St E\, Toronto\, ON\, M5E 1B4
URL:https://musictorontoconcerts.com/concerts/isserlis-shin
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
