SUMMARY:Royal Conservatory Orchestra with Conductor Earl Lee
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260501T200000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260501T200000
UID:988949b1ae1c04e076651e909bc97cae@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:A renowned Korean-Canadian cellist and conductor\, currently M
 usic Director of the Ann Arbor Symphony. He also served as assistant condu
 ctor of the Boston Symphony\, resident conductor of the Toronto Symphony O
 rchestra\, and associate conductor of the Pittsburgh Symphony. He is the 2
 022 recipient of The Sir Georg Solti Conducting Award.\n\nThe Temerty Orch
 estral Program at The Glenn Gould School\, the Royal Conservatory Orchestr
 a is widely regarded as an outstanding ensemble and one of the best traini
 ng orchestras in North America\, with graduates having joined the ranks of
  the greatest orchestras in the world.\n\nPlease join us! This concert is 
 preceded by a short performance by talented students of The Royal Conserva
 tory. \n\nCategories: Arts/Exhibits\, Live Performances\, Music
LOCATION:Koerner Hall\, Royal Conservatory of Music\, 273 Bloor St W\, Tor
 onto\, ON\, M5S 1W2
URL:https://www.rcmusic.com/events-and-performances/royal-conservatory-orc
 hestra-with-conductor-ea-(1)
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
