BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"City of Toronto Festivals & Events": "https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_festivals
SUMMARY:Inscape: Scarborough’s Shoreline Parks Exhibition
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260502T090000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260531T090000
UID:8551e37c18b56f125b89d7322a5bb053@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Examine the visual and material tension between wilderness and
  human control along Scarborough’s shoreline park system. Using traditio
 nal photographic techniques\, the work moves from representational landsca
 pe toward abstraction\, tracing how natural forces and urban intervention 
 shape one another over time. The project draws from repeated visits to sho
 reline parks\, beaches\, and wooded areas along the bluffs. \n\nAbout the 
 Artist\nChris is a Toronto-based photographer. Contemplative observation w
 ith a strong graphic sensibility for image making\, have come to represent
  his photographic style. His personal work can be found in corporate and p
 rivate collections throughout North America and Europe.\nCategories: Arts/
 Exhibits\nFree event
LOCATION:Clark Centre for the Arts\, 191 Guildwood Pkwy\, Scarborough\, ON
 \, M1E 1P5
URL:https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-cent
 res-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
