SUMMARY:Kerson Leong\, violin
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260503T151500
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260503T151500
UID:0bd9cb4946677f921573960af999e7d5@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Winner of the prestigious International Menuhin Violin Competi
 tion\, Kerson Leong has been described as “not just one of Canada’s gr
 eatest violinists but one of the greatest violinists\, period”. \n\nHe h
 as performed with Brussels\, Oslo\, Royal Philharmonic and Istanbul\, Sing
 apore\, Toronto\, Wuppertal and Montréal Symphony Orchestras. As a sought
 -after soloist\, Kerson has appeared at Carnegie and Wigmore Halls\, Audit
 orium du Louvre\, and National Center for the Performing Arts\, Beijing. \
 n\nHe plays the ‘ex Bohrer\, Baumgartner’ Guarneri del Gesu violin cou
 rtesy of Canimex Inc. Drummondville.\n\nHis virtuosic recital includes vio
 lin works by Ysaÿe (Sonata No. 3 “Ballade” & Sonata No. 4 in E minor)
 \, Kreisler’s Recitativo and Scherzo\, and Bach’s Chaconne from Partit
 a No. 2.\n\nCategories: Live Performances\, Music
LOCATION:Walter Hall\, University of Toronto\, 80 Queen's Park\, Toronto\,
  ON\, M5S 2C5
URL:https://www.mooredaleconcerts.com
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
