SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Board Game Café
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260512T200000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260512T220000Z
UID:69711d50992fc18a86deb18d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us in the Youth Hub every Tuesday to play board games wit
 h your friends! Ask us for our list of board games\, and check our monthly
  calendar for Tournaments with prizes! All materials provided.\nThis progr
 am is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teen
 s after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always availabl
 e. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\n
 Youth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Eatonville
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69711d50992fc18a86deb18d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69af3d918089f23c6760f85b"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Botanical Painting on Book Pages
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260512T200000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260512T220000Z
UID:69af3d918089f23c6760f85b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Turn pages of old discarded books into works of art in this mi
 x media workshop. Learn to create drawings and paintings of botanical obje
 cts such as flowers and berries in pen and watercolour. Whether you're a b
 eginner or an experienced artist\, you'll learn techniques for sketching b
 otanical subjects with fine pen details\, and then adding vibrant\, fluid 
 watercolours to bring them to life.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub ser
 vice. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school and in the s
 ummer\, where helpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious snack
 s are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the bran
 ch to find out more.
LOCATION:Cedarbrae\, Youth Hub\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69af3d918089f23c6760f85b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6999ffa3cbf1533ca537f20b"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:After School Fun
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260512T200000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260512T210000Z
UID:6999ffa3cbf1533ca537f20b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Spend your afternoon exploring STEM activities\, creating fun 
 crafts\, building with LEGO\, and making new friends — with something di
 fferent every week! For kids 6–12.\nDrop-in\, no registration required.\
 nFebruary 17: Robotics\nFebruary 24: Children's Graphic Novel Book Club\nM
 arch 3: LEGO\nMarch 10: Robotics\nMarch 24: Children's Graphic Novel Book 
 Club
LOCATION:High Park\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6999ffa3cbf1533ca537f20b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a8c194b48451fc3c06bf4f"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Music and AI for Kids!
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260512T200000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260512T210000Z
UID:69a8c194b48451fc3c06bf4f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for 4 weeks of goofy\, musical fun! Our Innovator in R
 esidence\, Joel S. Silver\, will show you how AI works to help you create 
 music. Create songs with the silliest lyrics you can think of\, create a s
 oundtrack for your own skits\, even write a theme song for the library! N
 o music or computer experience needed - just bring your creativity!\nFor a
 ges 8-12.\nDrop-in. No registration required\, but space is limited.\nThis
  program is part of the Innovator in Residence (AI and Music Production) p
 rogram\, which is designed to help beginner and intermediate learners buil
 d knowledge and creative skills and get hands-on with current AI tools in 
 music production and learn about the history\, copyright and ethics of gen
 erative music. For more information and a full list of programs\, visit\nt
 pl.ca/airesident\n.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a8c194b48451fc3c06bf4f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
