DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260516T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260516T110000
SUMMARY:FRC Toronto :: Saturday Run
DESCRIPTION:Founders Running Club :: Toronto\n**Founders Running Club** (FRC) brings founders\, investors\, tech\, creative people and startup enthusiasts together for weekly easy runs and networking. We like to be comfortable when we run and finish with coffee and conversations. Choose your pace or follow a pacer—pets\, friends\, family\, are welcome.\n\n🗓️ Launched in San Francisco\, July 16\, 2022\n🌍 Now in 35+ cities\n📅 Running + Networking events + Community\n\n**Join the community** https://bit.ly/frc-toronto-chat\n\n**Stay updated**:\nInstagram [http://instagram.com/foundersrc/](http://instagram.com/foundersrc/)\nPodcast [http://podcast.foundersrc.com/](http://podcast.foundersrc.com/)\nLinkedIn [http://linkedin.com/company/foundersrc/](http://linkedin.com/company/foundersrc/)\nStrava [http://strava.com/clubs/foundersRC](http://strava.com/clubs/foundersRC)\nWebsite [http://foundersrc.com/](http://foundersrc.com/)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/founders-running-club-toronto/events/kpqsrtyjchbvb/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20250607T041529Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20250607T041529Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/8/2/5/1/600_520173361.jpeg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"City of Toronto Festivals & Events": "https://www.rom.on.ca/whats-on/exhibitions/bees-story-survival?utm_source=cityoftoronto&utm_medium=listing&utm_campaign=bees"}
X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_festivals
SUMMARY:Bees: A Story of Survival
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260516T100000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260909T100000
UID:61e79956b771c15d15493a210ed0a375@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Bringing some buzz into your summer.\n\nJourney into the world
  of bees in a stunning new immersive experience that brings together the b
 eauty of art with the power of science. Created by the National Museums Li
 verpool in partnership with award-winning artist and sculptor\, Wolfgang B
 uttress\, the exhibition highlights 120-million years of bee adaptation an
 d survival\, telling the epic tale of these incredible creatures and their
  relationship to us and the natural world.\n\nBased on science and full of
  imagination\, the experiential exhibition presents a fusion of nature\, a
 rt\, music\, and architecture that transports visitors into the world of b
 ees - from the tiny\, fascinating anatomy of a single bee and the magical 
 wonder of honey bee colonies to the important roles bees play in our lives
  and the everyday threats they face.\n\nThrough immersive environments\, a
 rt installations\, soundscapes\, and more\, learn about the life of bees a
 nd the world they inhabit.\nCategories: Arts/Exhibits\, Environmental\, Mu
 seum
LOCATION:Royal Ontario Museum\, 100 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C6
URL:https://www.rom.on.ca/whats-on/exhibitions/bees-story-survival?utm_sou
 rce=cityoftoronto&utm_medium=listing&utm_campaign=bees
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
