X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup: High Park Yoga": "https://www.meetup.com/high-park-yoga/events/ghlfttyjchbwb/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_high_park_yoga
X-SOURCE:Meetup: High Park Yoga
UID:event_ghlfttyjchbwb@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260316T061703Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260517T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260517T110000
SUMMARY:Wild Breath Live on Zoom
DESCRIPTION:High Park Yoga\nI know so many of you enjoy the extended\, rythmic breathwork at the end of my yoga classes. Well\, here is your chance to continue harnessing the power of your breath guided by my patner Steve.\n\n**\\*\\*You must [sign up for free on Calendly via this link](https://calendly.com/breathinginnature/wild-breath) BEFORE the class to receive the Zoom link\\*\\***\n\n### What's the Wild Breath?\n\nOur breath is our most powerful healing tool & the energetic link between our mind\, body\, heart and spirit.\nIn this free\, one hour class guided by Steve live on Zoom you will use your breath to achieve a deep state of meditation and wellbeing. Breathing to the beats of the music\, you unlock the power within you to reduce stress and inflammation\, boost creativity\, release trapped emotions\, gain clarity and return to your true Self.\n\n**What you'll need:**\n\n* [Sign up for free on Calendly via this link](https://calendly.com/breathinginnature/wild-breath) **BEFORE** the class to receive the Zoom link\n* Good quality headphones or stereo system\n* Internet connection\n* A comfortable place to sit or lie down for your breathwork\n\n### Weekly\n\nTuesday 8pm EST\nWednesday 7am EST\nSunday 10am EST
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/high-park-yoga/events/ghlfttyjchbwb/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20250922T143603Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20250922T143603Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/6/8/7/600_530341671.jpeg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup: Sci Fi Book Club": "https://www.meetup.com/thescifibookclub/events/312949670/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_scifi_books
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Sci Fi Book Club
UID:event_312949670@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260316T061709Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260517T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260517T160000
SUMMARY:Her Smoke Rose Up Forever - James Tiptree Jr.
DESCRIPTION:The Sci Fi Book Club\nHi all\,\n\nFor May\, we will be reading another short story collection. Following April’s selection\, *Best American Science Fiction and Fantasy 2025*\, we’ll turn to an older anthology. This collection features stories by a science fiction writer who remained cloaked in mystery for years.\n\nBook of the Month\n*Her Smoke Rose Up Forever* \\- James Tiptree Jr\\. \\(1990\\)\n\nDirect from [this amazing Portalist](https://theportalist.com/james-tiptree-jr-enigmatic-author) article:\n"James Tiptree Jr. left an enduring mark on modern speculative fiction — but she’s perhaps more mysterious and enigmatic today than ever before.\n\nTiptree was one of the pen names used by female sci-fi author Alice Bradley Sheldon (née Alice Hastings Bradley). The daughter of prolific fiction writer Mary Hastings Bradley\, Sheldon may have been born with the gift of words\, but her path to literary success wasn’t clear-cut.\n\nAlthough Sheldon is best known for her sci-fi writing\, she had an eclectic and accomplished career. At various times in her life\, Sheldon was a research psychologist\, painter\, art critic\, imagery intelligence operative\, CIA operative\, and more. In many of these fields\, she was one of the few women in an industry dominated by men. "\n\nGiven this and Tiptree's well-known stories included in this collection\, I don't think we can pass up this opportunity. As with any other collection we read for Book Club\, if a story isn't speaking to you\, go ahead and skip it! There are 18 selections in here\, I'm sure we'll have plenty to discuss.\n\nBelow\, you'll find a few notables and a brief description:\n\n* “The Women Men Don’t See” – A classic feminist sci-fi story exploring gender\, invisibility\, and societal expectations.\n* “Houston\, Houston\, Do You Read?” – A Hugo Award–winning story about time travel\, gender\, and post-apocalyptic society.\n* “Love Is the Plan the Plan Is Death” – A highly acclaimed story told from the perspective of an alien species\, exploring instinct\, love\, and survival.\n* “The Girl Who Was Plugged In” – A groundbreaking cyberpunk-like story about identity\, media\, and corporate control of bodies.\n* “And I Awoke and Found Me Here on the Cold Hill’s Side” – A dark\, unsettling exploration of obsession and desire for alien contact.\n\nThere are a few printings of this collections. I think [I'm going to pick up this one](https://bookshop.org/p/books/her-smoke-rose-up-forever-james-tiptree/163a6a04d0124023?ean=9781892391209&next=t&utm_source=google&utm_medium=cpc&utm_campaign=%7Bcampaignname%7D&utm_content=6443417794&gad_source=1&gad_campaignid=16235479093&gbraid=0AAAAACfld43fka72FJRQfybRz8siTTDOZ&gclid=Cj0KCQiAprLLBhCMARIsAEDhdPdhUhUk1aiXVGaWtVIu9frZcido-IwCeX0rcqajtxQRQLphaxpwy68aAvCqEALw_wcB)\, as it includes some revisions from the author’s original notes.\n\nTo join a Book Club meeting\, all you will need is YOURSELF. If you haven’t had a chance to finish the book\, we still would love for you to join us in the discussion.\n\nNot able to join us in person for events? [The Sci Fi Book Club is on Discord](https://discord.gg/MM3hNQFW). Join us and keep the conversation going.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/thescifibookclub/events/312949670/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260119T002710Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260119T002710Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
