X-SOURCE:Meetup: These Boots Are Made for Hiking
UID:event_312915819@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260316T061659Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T120000
SUMMARY:Feel the burn folks on this Bike Ride led by ITALO!
DESCRIPTION:These Boots Are Made for Hiking\n**MEETUP POINT: Woodbine Park in front of the Beach Club - 1681 Lake Shore Blvd E**\nJoin us for a 50km bike ride in the city. Don't worry it's flat! Led by Italo who is an experienced cyclist and leader\, so you will be in good hands. It's lots of fun and not too far!\nThe ride begins at Woodbine park and ends nearby for a social and lunch. (I'll keep you posted on where it will be.)\nPlease come prepared with the right riding gear which means not a commuter bike.\nThis wouldn't be a beginner bike ride.\nBring lots of water and snacks.\nHelmets obviously a must!\n[https://ridewithgps.com/routes/53737876](https://ridewithgps.com/routes/53737876)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/these-boots-are-made-for-hiking/events/312915819/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260116T172056Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260116T172056Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/4/5/2/8/600_532277704.jpeg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup: Experience Toronto": "https://www.meetup.com/experiencetoronto/events/313011389/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_experience_to
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Experience Toronto
UID:event_313011389@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260316T061706Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T160000
SUMMARY:Penn & Teller Celebrate 50 Years of Magic + Pre-lunch (Union Station)
DESCRIPTION:Experience Toronto\nOn **Saturday June 6th**\, **let's Celebrate 50 Years of Magic with Penn & Teller.** Penn & Teller return to Toronto for the first time in 16 years with an unforgettable night of mind-blowing illusions\, sharp wit\, and legendary showmanship. Penn & Teller are a legendary magic act - Emmy\, Obie\, and Writer’s Guild Award-winning\, with stars on the Hollywood Walk of Fame. Penn & Teller know magic. Their CW TV show “Penn & Teller: Fool Us” has launched countless magic careers\, while successful Broadway runs and sold-out overseas tours have secured their place in the history books. My seat is ORCH10\, Row A\, Seat 83. **Please Purchase the newly added show on June 6th at 2pm show and post your seat number (caution there are other dates and times)**\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**REGULAR COST**\nTickets: $69 to $199 + ticket master fees\n\nOrganizer Meetup fee: $5\n\nTicket Policy: Final Sale - Non-Refundable & Non-Exchangeable. (You may opt to buy their insurance\, if you so desire.)\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**SIGNING-UP**\n\n* **RSVP Yes and answer the question about Lunch\, and the system will add you to the waitlist.**\n* **[Purchase your ticket](https://www.ticketmaster.ca/event/1000642FAD44DCCB?brand=tolive&CAMEFROM=CFC_TOLIVE_EMAIL_TOLIVE_E1&utm_source=TO+Live&utm_campaign=e0f9025468-EMAIL_CAMPAIGN_2026_01_19_04_29&utm_medium=email&utm_term=0_-e0f9025468-584141646&mc_cid=e0f9025468&mc_eid=96e408c1f2)**[ ](https://www.stratfordfestival.ca/WhatsOn/Calendar)and post your seat number\, so others may sit next to you.\n* I will then move you to attending\n\nRSVPs close 1 day prior and cancellations after may result in a No Show and impact future attendance.\n\nA reminder will be sent the day before with my cell and details where to meet and when.\n\n**MEETUP TIME**\n**Meet me for lunch at: 12pm inside the front doors of restaurant TBC at 33 Yonge St\,** Please wait for me to arrive\, and do not sit on your own prior\, so we can get the table requested.\n\n**Meet me for the show at 1:30pm** inside the 2nd set of glass front doors of Meridian Hall at 1 Front St. E. to the right side\, after scanning your tickets. We will aim to be in our seats 15 mins prior to catch an early start\n\n**Show start time: 2pm**\n\nShow length: estimate 90 mins\, there may be some interaction before and after\, per their website\, so arrive early\n\nEnjoy and please post your Comments in the event after.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/experiencetoronto/events/313011389/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260122T223609Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260122T223609Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/1/2/6/3/600_532384707.jpeg
END:VEVENT
